DSDA-Doom needs a game's IWAD
============================

No game data comes with DSDA-Doom. Put one of these in the DSDADoom
drawer (the names in lower case, as here):

  doom1.wad       Doom shareware (free to give away)
  doom.wad        The Ultimate Doom / Doom registered
  doom2.wad       Doom II
  tnt.wad         Final Doom: TNT Evilution
  plutonia.wad    Final Doom: The Plutonia Experiment
  freedoom1.wad   Freedoom Phase 1 (free, https://freedoom.github.io)
  freedoom2.wad   Freedoom Phase 2
  heretic.wad     Heretic (registered; the shareware heretic1.wad
                  with -iwad heretic1.wad -heretic)
  hexen.wad       Hexen

or name one: dsda-doom -iwad Work:WADs/doom2.wad
DOOMWADDIR and DOOMWADPATH (drawers separated by ';') are read from ENV:.

dsda-doom.wad, beside the program, is not an IWAD: it is DSDA-Doom's own
resource file (fonts, menu art, tables), built from its GPL sources, and
the game will not start without it.

PWADs are added with -file; demos are played with -playdemo, -timedemo
or -fastdemo.
